+/// A writer that records into this census, and where its pages came from.
+///
+/// The source decides what a release means to it. A rail that walked the
+/// task's live page table for this write found the page mapped at that moment:
+/// whatever the guest released earlier, the table names the page now, so the
+/// walk is the licence and the write is counted rather than reported (two
+/// soaks of an hour read about 1000 such writes, every one a page the guest had
+/// mapped again through a path this device does not observe). A rail writing
+/// through a page list it kept from an earlier resolve holds the page only
+/// through that list, and a release is exactly what retires the list.
